      "Battery projects without Wi-Fi"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Clone boards use the CH340 USB chip. Install the CH340 driver if no COM port appears.",
      "Upload fails? Choose Tools → Processor → ATmega328P (Old Bootloader).",
      "A6 and A7 are analog-input only; you can't use them with digitalRead or digitalWrite.",
      "Keep each pin under 20 mA. Drive relays, motors and LED strips through a transistor or module.",
      "The 3V3 pin on CH340 clones supplies very little current, so use an AMS1117-3.3 for 3.3V sensors.",
      "MQ gas sensors (~150 mA each), servos and motors need their own 5V supply, with grounds shared.",
      "Only 2 KB of SRAM: wrap fixed text in F(\"...\") inside Serial.print to save memory.",
      "D0/D1 are used by USB serial, so keep them free while uploading."
    ]
